---
title: 'Cone Funnel Series'
description: '$framework Cone Funnel Series shows the change of a value over a set of processes.'
---

A Cone Funnel Series illustrates how a value changes during a process, with a line representing the value at each stage
and filled areas denoting the change between them.

## Simple Cone Funnel

{% chartExampleRunner title="Cone Funnel Chart" name="simple-cone-funnel" type="generated" /%}

To create a Cone Funnel Series, use the `cone-funnel` series type.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'cone-funnel',
            stageKey: 'group',
            valueKey: 'value',
        },
    ],
}
```

In this configuration:

- `stageKey` defines the stages which are used for the lines of the cone funnel.
- `valueKey` provides the numerical values which determine the width of line.

## Horizontal Cone Funnel

{% chartExampleRunner title="Horizontal Cone Funnel Chart" name="horizontal-cone-funnel" type="generated" /%}

To create a horizontal Cone Funnel Series, set the `direction` to `horizontal`.

```js format="snippet"
{
    direction: 'horizontal',
}
```

## Customisation

{% chartExampleRunner title="Cone Funnel Fills" name="cone-funnel-fills" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    fills: ['#5090DC', '#FFA03A', '#459D55'],
}
```

In this configuration:

- The fills for each drop off area are defined in the `fills` array.
- The Cone Funnel series is reversed by providing the data items in the reverse order.

## Labels

The values can be displayed along the dividing line using the `label` option, and the stage names can be shown with the `stageLabel` option.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Cone Funnel Label Placement" name="cone-funnel-label-placement" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    label: {
        enabled: true,
        placement: 'middle-center',
    },
    stageLabel: {
        placement: 'before',
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

- The label defaults to `start-center`. Use the dropdown to see all available placements.
    - `start` and `end` are the two sides of the dividing line with `middle` sitting exactly on it.
    - `before`, `center` and `after` position the label along the length of the line.
- `stageLabel.placement` positions the stage names on either side of the chart.
- On a vertical cone funnel, `before` and `after` are mirrored when [RTL Layout](./rtl/) is enabled.

See [Series Labels](./series-labels/) for the full set of label placement and collision avoidance options, and the [API Reference](#api-reference) for additional customisation options.

